; Cranelisp Ring 4S — Sprint 61: Bare-primitive echo, observability, IO closure fix

(import [primitives [add-i64 mul-i64 not str-concat]])

; Sprint 61 delivered three user-visible wins: re-exported primitives now
; display a spec-conforming introspection card at the bare-value path;
; two new env-var-gated event logs (scheduler + IO) make concurrency
; bugs diagnosable instead of heisenbugs; and an IO-trampoline /
; closure-capture double-free (the `(fn [_] b)` / `bind` idiom) is
; now stable — the shape used in every `then`-style combinator.

; Slice 1 — bare-primitive name echo. Before S61, typing a re-exported
; primitive at the prompt errored "undefined variable: add-i64". The
; /int fix aligns three paths (bare value, /sig introspection, call)
; on the same terminal `primitives/add-i64` attribution per
; spec/08-modules.md §8.9. Type the name and the REPL answers
; per repl/spec.md §1.1: `:Type name ; classification - docstring`.

add-i64

/sig add-i64

(add-i64 2 3)

; A handful more — the fix generalises across the re-exported
; primitive surface (arithmetic, comparison, logical, string).

mul-i64

not

str-concat

; Slice 4 — capture-return-inc fix. The `(fn [_] b)` idiom at the heart
; of every `then`-style IO combinator previously double-freed the
; captured IO value: the closure returned `b` directly, the closure's
; drop-glue then dec'd `b`, and the outer trampoline read a poisoned
; tag. Surface symptoms ranged over exit codes 101, 133, 201, and
; SIGABRT — one root cause. The backend-side `emit_capture_return_inc`
; in control_flow.rs now balances the drop. The 7-line repro runs clean.

(import [primitives [Pure bind]])

(defn then [a b] (bind a (fn [_] b)))

(defn test-then [] (bind (then (Pure 999) (Pure 42)) (fn [x] (Pure (add-i64 x 8)))))

(test-then)

; Slice 0 — observability. Two env-var-gated event logs landed this
; sprint: CRANELISP_SCHEDULER_TRACE and CRANELISP_IO_TRACE. Each
; writes a merge-sortable dump to stderr at process exit — empty by
; default, zero-cost when unset. These logs were load-bearing during
; S61 Slice 3 root-causing (H4/H5/H6 race closures) and are now
; permanent instrumentation. See tests/CLAUDE.md §"Diagnostic Logging".

/sh printf 'CRANELISP_SCHEDULER_TRACE=1\nCRANELISP_IO_TRACE=1\n'

; Sample output (from sprint61 race-evidence logs) — one event per
; line, `(timestamp, thread_ord_id)`-sorted, per-thread ring buffers
; merged at process exit:
;
;   [SCH] ts=20007333 thr=ThreadId(2)/1 SymbolTableEnsure module=helper outcome=Created
;   [SCH] ts=20016083 thr=ThreadId(2)/1 SymbolTableEnsure module=helper outcome=AlreadyPresent
;   [SCH] ts=20024500 thr=ThreadId(1)/0 SymbolTableEnsure module=helper outcome=AlreadyPresent
;
; The "exactly one Created, all subsequent AlreadyPresent" pattern is
; the H6 atomicity invariant. Scheduler trace made this visible.

; Slice 3 — heisenbug race closures (infrastructure). Three scheduler
; races closed this sprint (H4 publish-vs-flag ordering, H5 REPL-eval
; thread starvation, H6 non-atomic ensure_module_exists). The fixes are
; not directly demoable from the prompt — but the new trace above is
; the tooling that made them tractable. Same source, same code bytes,
; now across JIT finalize and .o relocation, and now across concurrent
; module-registration windows.

; Sprint 61 closes: 1 bare-primitive path convergence, 2 trace event
; streams, 3 race closures, 1 IO-closure double-free repaired. Path
; clear for Sprint 62's FQTypeName migration.
